{# BREADCRUMB LEAF — the label for the current page (final crumb).
   Default = the page title. Per-type enrichment lives here:
   - jam → "Song by Artist", with a serif-italic "by" and the artist un-wikilinked.
     The artist is plain text for now (no artist archive exists yet — no dead link).
   - watching / reading → the same "by" shape, with the film's director or the book's
     author. Both fields may be a single name or a list, with or without [[wikilinks]].
   - activity → "Orienteering: Mok Torsdag Bokskogen" — activityType + colon prefixed
     onto the title, plain (no connector styling; activityType is stored lowercase;
     capitalize it).
   - the link cohort (like / bookmark / reply / repost) → "Title on Source", where
     Source is ALWAYS the bare host of whichever URL field that type uses — e.g.
     "arielsalminen.com" — never sourceName. RSVP is deliberately NOT in the cohort:
     its title already says what it is a reply to, so the host only repeats it.
   Keep the markup minimal; the surrounding <span aria-current="page"> + truncation
   live in breadcrumb.njk / breadcrumb.css. The plain `breadcrumbs[].label` (used for
   aria/JSON-LD) stays the raw title — only this *visible* leaf is enriched. #}
{%- set linkedHost = (sourceUrl or likeOf or bookmarkOf or inReplyTo or repostOf) | hostname -%}
{%- if category == "jam" and artist -%}
  {{ title }} <span class="breadcrumb-connector">by</span> {{ artist | unwikilink }}
{%- elif (category == "watching" and director) or (category == "reading" and author) -%}
  {%- set byline = director if category == "watching" else author -%}
  {{ title }} <span class="breadcrumb-connector">by</span> {% if byline is string %}{{ byline | unwikilink }}{% else %}{{ byline | unwikilink | join(", ") }}{% endif %}
{%- elif category == "activity" and activityType -%}
  {# activityType is an English controlled term ("orienteering") — only the title may be
     Swedish, so lang="sv" (set by titleLang, see eleventyComputed.js) wraps the title alone. #}
  {{ activityType | capitalize }}: {% if titleLang %}<span lang="{{ titleLang }}">{{ title }}</span>{% else %}{{ title }}{% endif %}
{%- elif category == "audio" and place -%}
  {# Field recordings title the SUBJECT ("Small waves"), so the crumb composes it with
     where it was recorded: "Small waves at Nybrostrand". "at" carries almost every
     named location; a post that wants "in"/"on" (a forest, a train) sets placePreposition.
     `region` is deliberately left out — the leaf truncates to one line in the header, so it
     would be the first thing lost, and it already appears in the recording details. #}
  {{ title }} <span class="breadcrumb-connector">{{ placePreposition or "at" }}</span> {{ place }}
{%- elif category in ["like", "bookmark", "reply", "repost"] and (linkedHost) -%}
  {{ title }} <span class="breadcrumb-connector">on</span> {{ linkedHost }}
{%- elif tag -%}
  {# Tag archive pages: show the bare tag, not the page title "Tag: <x>". #}
  {{ tag }}
{%- else -%}
  {{ title }}
{%- endif -%}
